### Limitations the authors admit
- 2018ApJ...868..113T: Resolution (~29 au) leaves velocity features unresolved, underestimating depth
- 2018ApJ...868..113T: Cannot disentangle pressure gradient from stellar mass; pressure scaling depends on assumed density
- 2019ApJ...873...73Z: Model is simple and illustrative; geometry, abundance and excitation simplified
- 2019ApJ...873...73Z: Resolution too low to get detailed disk rotation profile
- 2025ApJ...994...98F: Surface bias and limited number of lines per annulus prevent discriminating between vertical temperature prescriptions
- 2021A&A...648A..19W: Posterior uncertainties are small and likely underestimated; systematic model uncertainties
- 2021A&A...648A..19W: Pitch angles are only rough estimates from by-eye spiral parameterization
- 2012ApJ...757..129R: Model parameters are not unique nor optimized; limited resolution
- 2025SciA...11.4512O: Mass of ALMA1 is an upper limit under optically thin approximation; infall is neither free-fall nor viscous
- 2025SciA...11.4512O: Red-shifted streamer excluded from methanol analysis due to outflow contamination
- 2014ApJ...786..114L: Disk is not well resolved, so its radius is an upper limit and the temperature index is rough; model is simple and symmetric and excludes outflow, jet and extended envelope.
- 2016ApJ...829....6W: CO mass assumes optically thin LTE and could be larger by a factor of a few or more
- 2016ApJ...829....6W: Debris mass depends strongly on assumed size distribution, density, albedo
- 2020ApJ...898...10T: Model CBD larger than observed; magnetic field not included; high-velocity blueshifted components near Source N not reproduced; infall not identified observationally
- 2018A&A...614A.113H: Parameters tuned visually; no statement on fit quality
- 2018A&A...614A.113H: Insufficient spatial resolution limits kinematics
- 2013ApJ...776...77K: Inner radius only an upper limit; brightness exponent ill-determined; full radiative transfer model postponed
- 2017ApJ...837...93Y: Orbit not determined a priori; line-of-sight velocity and position unknown
- 2015ApJ...811...39I: 150 pc resolution mixes AGN and SB contributions; CO(3-2) only partially covered
- 2020ApJ...892...99C: Temperature poorly constrained by the data
- 2020ApJ...892...99C: Calibration uncertainty not included in MCMC fit
- 2026A&A...705A.198M: Optically thick masses are lower limits; inner radii are upper limits; degeneracy thick/thin needs radiative transfer
- 2018ApJ...864..133T: Beam smear not corrected, affecting inner 90-100 au
- 2018ApJ...864..133T: Neighbouring annuli are correlated within a beam
- 2018ApJ...864L..25O: Mass may be an upper limit or apparent value because of non-Keplerian gravity and unresolved material
- 2024MNRAS.534.2904C: Residuals are model dependent; Keplerian background assumed
- 2020ApJ...891...48H: Temperature, flux calibration and degeneracies prevent precise grain size measurements
- 2013ApJ...774...16R: Models are degenerate, not unique or optimal; systematic residuals at large radii
- 2013ApJ...774...16R: Band 7 sky frequency in SV measurement set incorrect
- 2025NatAs...9.1833L: Masses are lower limits due to optical depth and missing flux
- 2025NatAs...9.1833L: Secondary disks cannot be confirmed with current sensitivity and resolution
- 2015ApJ...812...27A: Inclination poorly constrained by the disk model; mass estimates are uncertain by optical depth, temperature, abundance
- 2015ApJ...812...27A: PV mean-position method underestimates break radius at limited resolution
- 2017ApJ...842....8M: Resolution (~10 AU) prevents constraints on edge sharpness; Δa and e_p degenerate; large uncertainty on ω from inclination degeneracy
- 2017ApJ...842....8M: 2D model ignores vertical structure, which could loosen width constraints
- 2020ApJ...893...51S: Outer disk inclination cannot be measured independently; non-axisymmetry not modeled
- 2018A&A...614A..58B: Inner disk and width poorly constrained; mass depends on CO abundance and distance; LTE assumption; temperature uncertain
- 2015MNRAS.447.3936M: Detailed chemical modelling beyond scope; T_k assumed uniform; vibrational/electronic states neglected
