  - assumption: Black hole mass 1.7e6 Msun; Keplerian rotation [4.3 Possible Detection of High-velocity…: "for a 1.7 $\times$ 10$^6$ $M_{\ensuremath{\odot}}\;$black hole"]
- result: Radius of high-velocity feature = ~0.018 ± not stated pc [4.3 Possible Detection of High-velocity…: "it is located at a radius of $\sim$ 0.018 pc"]
- limitation (authors): Beam too large to measure brightness temperature or resolve kinematics [4.1 Origin: "The synthesized beam size of our observation was too large to determine if the detected 321 GHz H$_{2}$O$\;$emission is thermal emission or maser"]
- not stated (card): CASA version; Line-free channel ranges; Clean threshold, cell and image size, masking; Flux density of Titan model and phase-reference solutions; Which antennas/baselines and any flagging; Number of channels averaged or velocity resolution of images; Details of Gaussian fits

