### 2019A&A...632L..12H: Multiple nitrogen reservoirs in a protoplanetary disk at the epoch of comet and giant planet formation (2019; protoplanetary_disks, astrochemistry; archival_reuse)
- question: Do HCN and CN trace distinct nitrogen isotopic reservoirs in the TW Hya disk, and does HCN/HC15N vary with radius (selective photodissociation)?
- step 2: Spatially averaged line fluxes in Keplerian masks
  - method: Mask where HCN 354507.455 MHz hf line >40 mJy/beam per channel, exclude r<0.3''; average spectra; Gaussian fit weak hf lines; HCN flux = average corrected by 4.2% relative intensity [4.1 Spatially averaged line fluxes: "selecting the disk area where the 354507.455 MHz hyperfine emission of HCN is higher than 40 mJy/beam in each velocity channel"]
  - software: Gildas
  - parameter: threshold 40 mJy/beam; r>0.3'' [4.1 Spatially averaged line fluxes: "we further masked out the spectra located at radii smaller than 0.3$''$"]
  - assumption: Optically thin lines, equal excitation temperature, flux ratio = column density ratio within 1% [5 Isotopic ratios: "their rotational flux ratios are equal to their column density ratios to within 1%, provided the lines are optically thin and have the same excitation temperature"]
  - fitting: Gaussian fitting [4.1 Spatially averaged line fluxes: "were measured through Gaussian fitting"]
  - validation: Opacity corrections tau/(1-exp(-tau)) tested; HCN/H13CN near constant [5 Isotopic ratios: "the almost constant HCN/H suggests that these lines are instead optically thin"]
- step 3: Radial profile of isotopic ratios
  - method: Combine Keplerian and annular masks, 5 au wide annuli from 5 to 55 au in 5 au steps, rms-weighted averaging, Gaussian fits; power law fit to HCN/HC15N [4.2 Radially dependent fluxes: "Spectra contained within concentric annuli, centered at radii $r=5$ to 55 au in steps of 5 au"]
  - software: Gildas
  - parameter: distance 59.5 pc [4.2 Radially dependent fluxes: "we adopted a distance of 59.5$\pm$0.9 pc to TW Hya"]
  - fitting: Power law to HCN/HC15N [5 Isotopic ratios: "The best fit of a power law to the HCN/HC gives 117$\pm$10$\times(r/20\,\au)^{1.3\pm0.13}$"]
  - validation: Ratios change <4% excluding three central channels [5 Isotopic ratios: "The ratios change by less than 4% when the three central Keplerian channels are excluded."]
- result: Average HCN/HC15N = 223 ± 21 dimensionless [Table 1: "| Average | 223$\pm$21 | 86$\pm$4 | 2.6$\pm$0.2 |"]
- result: Average HCN/H13CN = 86 ± 4 dimensionless [Table 1: "| Average | 223$\pm$21 | 86$\pm$4 | 2.6$\pm$0.2 |"]
- result: HCN/HC15N at 20 au = 121.4 ± 10.6 dimensionless [Table 1: "| $r$ (au)=20 | 121.4$\pm$10.6 | 85.6$\pm$ 5.2 | 1.4$\pm$0.1 |"]
- result: HCN/HC15N at 45 au = 338.7 ± 28.2 dimensionless [Table 1: "| 45 | 338.7$\pm$28.2 | 82.5$\pm$ 4.2 | 4.2$\pm$0.4 |"]
- result: Power-law fit to HCN/HC15N = 117×(r/20 au)^1.3 ± ±10 amplitude, ±0.13 index dimensionless [5 Isotopic ratios: "The best fit of a power law to the HCN/HC gives 117$\pm$10$\times(r/20\,\au)^{1.3\pm0.13}$"]
- limitation (authors): Detailed 2D radiative transfer not done; ratio beyond 55 au tentative [Single excitation temperature assumption: "In the present context, we were unable to make detailed calculations like this."]
- not stated (card): Imaging parameters (weighting, robust, cell, image size, beam) not given; Self-calibration solution intervals and reference model; Which array configurations/execution blocks were combined; Continuum subtraction and line-free channels; Gaussian fit details and Keplerian mask construction details beyond threshold; Disk inclination and position angle used for radii; Details of ALICO collisional rat…

### 2017ApJ...849...56A: ALMA Observations of the Protostar L1527 IRS: Probing Details of the Disk and the Envelope Structures (2017; star_formation, protoplanetary_disks; observational_alma_primary)
- question: Can the disk and envelope around the protostar L1527 IRS be distinguished kinematically and geometrically, and what are their structures?
