  - assumption: Keplerian rotation; geometry fixed from earlier work [main text: "We assumed the disk material orbits the central star in Keplerian motion"]
  - fitting: chi2 grid search, 3 sigma errors [Table S2: "Errors within 3$\sigma$."]
  - validation: repeated for each z_big; inner radius varies <5 AU; residual channel maps [N2H+ line modeling: "Across this range of models, the inner radius varies by less than 5 AU"]
- result: N2H+ inner radius (fiducial z_big=3H) = 30 ± +1/-2 (3 sigma) AU [Table S2: "| 3.0 | 30$^{+1}_{-2}$ | 16–17"]
- result: N2H+ column density at 100 AU (z_big=3H) = 1.6e14 ± 0.3e14 cm^-2 [Table S2: "(1.6$\pm$0.3) $\times$10$^{14}$"]
- result: N2H+ outer radius (z_big=3H) = 140 ± 10 AU [Table S2: "| 3.0 | 30$^{+1}_{-2}$ | 16–17 | $-$2.0$^{+0.5}_{-0.7}$ | (1.6$\pm$0.3) $\times$10$^{14}$ | 140$\pm$10 |"]
- limitation (authors): Vertical disk structure is uncertain; vertical N2H+ boundaries fixed [Physical model: "The details of the vertical structure in the TW Hya disk are therefore uncertain"]
- not stated (card): Imaging parameters (weighting, robust, cell, image size, masking, deconvolver); Line-free channel selection and self-cal solution intervals; Grid ranges and step sizes for Rin, Rout, p, N100; Full disk model density/temperature structure files; Flux scale uncertainty for the ALMA data

